{"title":"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 25","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For each integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/0/6d034b51294ef53e016b9d7fefd837a865e52d2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\geq 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1a2b6b7c193f9ba2b2134a59f1da5addcfbc98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"13\" /> denote the base-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/9/94955dabf51a58a99d620be595fe8f76c1fed7e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.\\overline{133}_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"49\" height=\"17\" />. The product <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/c/32c613b71010035e4172dfe1fb4b952af14972d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_4a_5\\cdots a_{99}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"83\" height=\"10\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/9/1e9e139a14911866cbc0ed0733fafc93ed9828c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {m}{n!}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"18\" height=\"33\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are positive integers and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is as small as possible. What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/3/8537979f216242f8c3042329a94920aa7e8d38f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text {(A)} 98 \\qquad \\text {(B)} 101 \\qquad \\text {(C)} 132\\qquad \\text {(D)} 798\\qquad \\text {(E)}962$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"384\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>This is an infinite <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Geometric_series\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Geometric series\">geometric series</a> with common ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/c/16cbf94dd75d7e1d5f7bab6ff540b085826ad77c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{x^3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" /> and initial term <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/5/515bb31b17af15c0c6fc74dbf81b7065e37291ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{-1} + 3x^{-2} + 3x^{-3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"146\" height=\"16\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/0/0e0695b2f3eb4e2240b38d0863b274d651134df3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_x = \\left(\\frac{1}{x} + \\frac{3}{x^2} + \\frac{3}{x^3}\\right)\\left(\\frac{1}{1-\\frac{1}{x^3}}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"249\" height=\"45\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/b/f3bb744f9930e9fdb9c8a884cf0b76376fcdba15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= \\frac{x^2 + 3x + 3}{x^3} \\cdot \\frac{x^3}{x^3 - 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"178\" height=\"39\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/f/52f7a33bbaf653a2718b0fafde37e2fef8904404.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= \\frac{x^2 + 3x + 3}{x^3 - 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"112\" height=\"39\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/a/27a3cd93be79b63df77dd900cbe6a4d794bb8895.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= \\frac{(x+1)^3 - 1}{x(x^3 - 1)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"116\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p><p>Alternatively, we could have used the algebraic manipulation for repeating decimals, \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/2/f023e74460b3c730d118447967e7f6d1fa6e661b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} a_x &amp;= \\frac{1}{x}+\\frac{3}{x^2}+\\frac{3}{x^3}+\\frac{1}{x^4}+\\frac{3}{x^5}+\\frac{3}{x^6}+\\cdots \\\\ a_x \\cdot x^3 &amp;= x^2+3x+3+a_x\\\\ a_x(x^3-1) &amp;= x^2+3x+3\\\\ a_x &amp;= \\frac{x^2+3x+3}{x^3-1}=\\frac{(x+1)^3-1}{x(x^3-1)} \\end{align*}\" width=\"381\" height=\"142\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Telescoping\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Telescoping\">Telescoping</a>, \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/0/580618e7c0cd904ca791d38be470ebde43342988.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} a_4a_5\\cdots a_{99}&amp;= \\frac{(5^3-1)(6^3-1)\\cdots (100^3-1)}{4 \\cdot 5 \\cdot 6 \\cdot \\cdots \\cdot 99 \\cdot (4^3-1)(5^3-1)\\cdots(99^3-1)}\\\\ a_4a_5\\cdots a_{99}&amp;= \\frac{999999}{4 \\cdot 5 \\cdot 6 \\cdot \\cdots \\cdot 99 \\cdot 63}=\\frac{13 \\cdot 37 \\cdot 33 \\cdot 6}{99!}\\end{align*}\" width=\"466\" height=\"87\" />\n</p><p>Some factors cancel, (after all, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c7e40ee2ffe8b5f8ec0898d2da93d56515ecca2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13 \\cdot 37 \\cdot 33 \\cdot 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"102\" height=\"13\" /> isn't one of the answer choices)\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/8/52810daca693273a5f69bfa46b11f70a730759a9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{13 \\cdot 37 \\cdot 33 \\cdot 6}{99!}=\\frac{13 \\cdot 37 \\cdot 2}{98!}\\]\" width=\"203\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Since the only factor in the numerator that goes into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/1/73119f04d6ae5f6eb4afc8c9c946a5744a11be50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$98$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is minimized. Therefore the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/4/114b8acae2d762b64c1f81dcdd23919140d1fd56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13 \\cdot 37 \\cdot 2=962 \\Rightarrow \\text {(E)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"174\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/1/5515d34ff47fe7730ad2872fdaf7bd36f2fe557d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[0.\\overline{133}_n = \\frac{n^2+3n+3}{n^3-1},\\]\" width=\"174\" height=\"39\" />by geometric series.\nThus, we're aiming to find the value of<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/e/67e270e2d083dd4dce4e9acc3f793d437362f5d0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\prod_{k=4}^{99} \\frac{k^2+3k+3}{k^3 - 1}.\\]\" width=\"124\" height=\"50\" />Expanding the product out, this is equivalent to\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/b/fdbc97466d7e7c98aeedc597122d6c3d3dc7cf06.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{4^2+3(4)+3}{4^3 - 1} \\cdot \\frac{5^2+3(5)+3}{5^3 - 1} \\cdot \\frac{6^2+3(6)+3}{6^3 - 1} \\cdot ... \\cdot \\frac{99^2+3(99)+3}{99^3 - 1}.\\]\" width=\"480\" height=\"39\" />Note that the numerator of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />th fraction and the denominator of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/b/64be5731bafe97ab8fb5d0f9c52c1c5362f963d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" />th fraction for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/2/4f25b2323b1014854bd54d77a7cf1b1f666b4f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\leq a \\leq 95$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"84\" height=\"15\" /> cancel out to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/d/83dde6bf635bb1c7aac5cad1328d5240203e0113.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{a+3},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"49\" height=\"38\" /> since<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/c/9cce8bcb11a2f7ba2512db00a5e1ec243533553e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{k^2 + 3k + 3}{(k+1)^3 - 1} = \\frac{k^2 + 3k + 3}{k^3 + 3k^2 + 3k} = \\frac{1}{k},\\]\" width=\"274\" height=\"43\" />by the binomial theorem on the the denominator of the aforementioned. Since this forms a telescoping series, our product is now equivalent to<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/f/79fe4bc33aedfb1a1f5cb5e0705d5f4466cac7e1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{99^2 + 3(99) + 3}{4^3 - 1} \\cdot \\prod_{k=4}^{98} \\frac{1}{k},\\]\" width=\"181\" height=\"50\" />which, after simplification gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/b/beb78d55e18c0beb1ddf122af3a71f04d6c9de82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{6}{98!} \\cdot \\frac{10101}{63} = \\frac{962}{98!},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"149\" height=\"37\" /> giving an answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/9/789c2e0453f480ccf4bc112f2d27e2eee5fb4acd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{962}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p>-fidgetboss_4000\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A\">2004 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 24\">Problem 24</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last Question</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261016235443\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.041 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.061 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 275/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2264/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 162/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7584/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.820      1 -total\n 54.67%    7.556      1 Template:AMC12_box\n 43.78%    6.050      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:5908:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261016235443 and revision id 131986. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}